From 33ab8a639b4e1c7c1ef58cbd622d44fb8cb8ea43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 04:30:36 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] [mpegts] Keep the parameter sets of a stream across a
 parser reset

A seek resets the parsers at the PES of the key frame. The H.264 and
HEVC parsers then dropped every frame until the next SPS and PPS, so a
seek to an IDR or IRAP picture that uses the parameter sets of an
earlier picture ended the stream. The decoder keeps the parameter sets
in the extra data, so the parsers now keep them too. A reset still
waits for a key frame: H.264 waits for an I slice as before, and HEVC
now waits for an IRAP picture, which the SPS gate did before.

MPEG-2 has no parameter sets outside the stream, and a decoder can
start only at a sequence header. The parser keeps the need for a
sequence header after a reset, and a seek now lands only on an I
picture after a sequence header.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
